    <section class="rise-fall" id="timeline" aria-labelledby="timeline-title">
      <h2 class="profile-section-title" id="timeline-title">Timeline</h2>
      <ol class="rf-events"><li><span class="rf-year">1930</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haile-selassie">Haile Selassie</a> is crowned Emperor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a>, and several Jamaican clergymen claim that it fulfils biblical prophecy and shows that he is a black messiah</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1934</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jamaica">Jamaica</a>'s colonial authorities arrest Leonard Howell and charge him with sedition, and he is imprisoned for two years</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1939</span><span class="rf-text">Howell forms a Rasta community known as Pinnacle in Saint Catherine Parish, which the police raid repeatedly and which closes in 1954</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1958</span><span class="rf-text">After the first Rastafarian Universal Convention in Back-o-Wall, Kingston, Rasta militants unsuccessfully try to capture the city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haile-selassie">Haile Selassie</a>'s name</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1966</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haile-selassie">Haile Selassie</a> visits <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jamaica">Jamaica</a> at its government's invitation, and thousands of Rastas gather to see his arrival at the airport</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1975</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haile-selassie">Haile Selassie</a> dies a year after his overthrow by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/derg">Derg</a>, which causes a crisis of faith for many practitioners</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1982</span><span class="rf-text">The first international assembly of Rastafari groups takes place in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toronto">Toronto</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">2015</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jamaica">Jamaica</a> decriminalises personal possession of marijuana up to two ounces</span></li></ol>
    </section>

